    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nCalling `vim.pack.get` causes the test case to not report anything, neither success, nor failure.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n\n    vim.cmd([[let &rtp.=','.getcwd()]])\n    require('mini.test').setup()\n    ```\n\n3. Create a test file at `tests/test_vim.pack.get.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    local T = MiniTest.new_set()\n    T[\"vim.pack.get\"] = function()\n        vim.pack.get()\n        MiniTest.expect.equality(true, false) -- should report failure\n    end\n    return T\n    ```\n\n4. Run\n\n    ```sh\n    NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim --headless -c \"lua MiniTest.run()\"\n    ```\n\n5. Headless test reports nothing. Interactive test with the UI correctly reports `Fail`.\n\n<details><summary>What to do after reporting an issue</summary>\n\nAfter reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n\n</details>\n",
