            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce. It might have to do with the fact that `vim.pack.get()` by default asynchronously collects data from plugins but waits for them to finish. This probably somehow interferes with 'mini.test' collection lifecycle. Using `vim.pack.get(nil, { info = false })` doesn't have this behavior.\n\nI 'll take a look.\n\n> But here is a workaround:\n\nThis is not quite a workaround, but a suggested way to actually test `vim.pack.get()` behavior. All tested calls are better to be done inside child process.",
