        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`.\n\nThe reason was that all collected test cases were meant to be executed in their order by `vim.schedule()`-ing them in order. This works most of the times, but if some case calls async-adjacent function (like `vim.wait` or `vim.pack.get()`), then it can go through other scheduled functions. This compromises assumed order and might result into `reporter.finish` be executed not last.\n\nI remember wanting to fix this a year or two ago, but decided to not increase complexity as it worked as is. Glad that my instinct was right back then, not glad that I did not listen to it :)",
